(2) THE BOUNDS
  Bekenstein  S_Bek(r) = 2 pi k_B M_ph(<r) r c/hbar  [in k_B units: 2 pi M_ph c r/hbar]
    at r_M, on the contained phantom mass M_ph(<r_M) = M_b:  S_Bek = 7.8346e+104 k_B
    (using the total enclosed mass M_b + M_ph = 2 M_b doubles it to 1.5669e+105 -- irrelevant to the verdict)
  Bekenstein-Hawking of the contained mass (self-gravity cap the bound converges to):  S_BH = 5.1422e+98 k_B
  Area-law entropy on the sphere at r_M:  S_holo(r_M) = 1.1937e+111 k_B
  de Sitter horizon (Z11, R_dS = 5.3742 Gpc):  S_dS = pi c^3 R_dS^2/(hbar G) = A_dS/(4 l_P^2) = 3.3074e+122 k_B

  THE RATIOS at r_M (m = 5.09 keV):
    S_ph(<r_M)/S_Bek(r_M)        = 4.277e-31  (integral) / 4.669e-31 (product)
